# 5. Two Types of Tree BFS

## Type 1: Simple BFS

Use this when the problem only asks you to visit every node in BFS order.

```java
class Solution {

    public List<Integer> bfs(TreeNode root) {

        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            TreeNode node = queue.poll();

            result.add(node.val);

            if (node.left != null) {
                queue.offer(node.left);
            }

            if (node.right != null) {
                queue.offer(node.right);
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

This returns:

```text
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
```

It does not separate nodes by level.

---

## Type 2: Level-by-Level BFS

Use this when the problem asks about:

- Each level
- Maximum of every level
- Average of every level
- Right-side view
- Left-side view
- Zigzag order
- Minimum depth
- Connecting nodes on the same level

```java
while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

    int levelSize = queue.size();

    for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {

        TreeNode node = queue.poll();

        if (node.left != null) {
            queue.offer(node.left);
        }

        if (node.right != null) {
            queue.offer(node.right);
        }
    }
}
```

