# 7. Universal Tree BFS Template

```java
class Solution {

    public ReturnType bfs(TreeNode root) {

        // Handle an empty tree.
        if (root == null) {
            // Return the appropriate empty/default answer.
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            // Number of nodes in the current level.
            int levelSize = queue.size();

            // Initialize information required for this level.
            // Examples: level list, sum, maximum, previous node.

            for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {

                TreeNode node = queue.poll();

                // Perform problem-specific work here.

                // Add children for the next level.
                if (node.left != null) {
                    queue.offer(node.left);
                }

                if (node.right != null) {
                    queue.offer(node.right);
                }
            }

            // Complete the current level's calculation here.
        }

        // Return the final answer.
    }
}
```

The BFS structure normally remains the same.

Only the **problem-specific work** changes.

