# 14. LeetCode 103: Zigzag Level Order Traversal

## Problem idea

Traversal direction changes after every level.

```text
Level 0: left to right
Level 1: right to left
Level 2: left to right
```

We can still perform normal BFS.

Only the insertion position inside the level list changes.

## Code

```java
class Solution {

    public List<List<Integer>> zigzagLevelOrder(TreeNode root) {

        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        boolean leftToRight = true;

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            int levelSize = queue.size();
            LinkedList<Integer> currentLevel = new LinkedList<>();

            for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {

                TreeNode node = queue.poll();

                if (leftToRight) {
                    currentLevel.addLast(node.val);
                } else {
                    currentLevel.addFirst(node.val);
                }

                if (node.left != null) {
                    queue.offer(node.left);
                }

                if (node.right != null) {
                    queue.offer(node.right);
                }
            }

            result.add(currentLevel);

            // Reverse the direction for the next level.
            leftToRight = !leftToRight;
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

## Pattern change

```java
boolean leftToRight = true;
```

For left-to-right:

```java
currentLevel.addLast(node.val);
```

For right-to-left:

```java
currentLevel.addFirst(node.val);
```

After every level:

```java
leftToRight = !leftToRight;
```

