# 15. LeetCode 116: Populating Next Right Pointers

## Important node difference

This problem uses `Node`, not `TreeNode`.

```java
class Node {
    int val;
    Node left;
    Node right;
    Node next;
}
```

The `next` pointer should connect nodes on the same level.

```text
4 → 5 → 6 → 7 → null
```

## Code

```java
class Solution {

    public Node connect(Node root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return null;
        }

        Queue<Node> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            int levelSize = queue.size();

            // Tracks the previously processed node
            // on the current level.
            Node previous = null;

            for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {

                Node currentNode = queue.poll();

                if (previous != null) {
                    previous.next = currentNode;
                }

                previous = currentNode;

                if (currentNode.left != null) {
                    queue.offer(currentNode.left);
                }

                if (currentNode.right != null) {
                    queue.offer(currentNode.right);
                }
            }

            // Last node of the current level points to null.
            previous.next = null;
        }

        return root;
    }
}
```

## Connection dry run

Current level:

```text
[4, 5, 6, 7]
```

Processing:

```text
previous = null, current = 4
No connection yet
previous = 4
```

```text
previous = 4, current = 5
4.next = 5
previous = 5
```

```text
previous = 5, current = 6
5.next = 6
previous = 6
```

```text
previous = 6, current = 7
6.next = 7
previous = 7
```

After the level:

```text
7.next = null
```

Final connections:

```text
4 → 5 → 6 → 7 → null
```

