# 19. Time and Space Complexity

For a tree containing `n` nodes:

## Time complexity

```text
O(n)
```

Every node is:

- Added to the queue once
- Removed from the queue once
- Processed once

## Space complexity

```text
O(w)
```

`w` is the maximum width of the tree.

The maximum width is the largest number of nodes present in the queue around one level.

Worst case:

```text
O(n)
```

